  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "When the circumference of a toy balloon is increased from \\(20\\) inches to \\(25\\) inches, the radius is increased by:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(5\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\dfrac12\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac5\\pi\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{2\\pi}\\) in"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}\\) in"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p34.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(C=2\\pi r,\\) the changes satisfy \\[ 25-20=2\\pi\\mathopen{}\\left(r_{\\mathrm{new}}-r_{\\mathrm{old}}\\right)\\mathclose{}. \\] Hence the radius increases by \\(\\dfrac{5}{2\\pi}\\) inches.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(C=2\\pi r\\) for each circumference",
        "The change in circumference is \\(2\\pi\\) times the change in radius"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
